---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import ContentNote from '../components/content/ContentNote.astro';
import RelatedReading from '../components/content/RelatedReading.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | Cooked Finance"
  description="How Cooked Finance plans, researches, writes, reviews, labels, updates, and corrects educational personal-finance content."
  path="/editorial-policy"
  eyebrow="Trust and accountability"
  heading="Our editorial policy."
  lead="Useful personal-finance content should show its evidence, its assumptions, and its limits."
  updated="August 17, 2026"
>
  <h2>Purpose and scope</h2>
  <p>
    Cooked Finance is an independent educational website. We publish calculators,
    model documentation, data explainers, and practical guides intended to help
    readers ask clearer questions about their money. We do not provide personal
    financial, investment, tax, legal, credit, or accounting advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Our editorial standards</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Be useful before being searchable.</strong> A page should solve a defined reader problem rather than exist only to target a keyword.</li>
    <li><strong>Separate evidence from our model.</strong> Published statistics, external guideposts, and Cooked Finance scoring choices are labelled distinctly.</li>
    <li><strong>Prefer original utility.</strong> Calculators, transparent formulas, worksheets, tables, and careful synthesis should add something beyond summarizing another page.</li>
    <li><strong>Use primary sources.</strong> Regulators, government datasets, statutes, official documentation, and original research are preferred where available.</li>
    <li><strong>Avoid false precision.</strong> We do not manufacture percentiles, probabilities, projections, or authoritative-sounding thresholds from insufficient evidence.</li>
    <li><strong>Write without shame.</strong> Financial difficulty is not a character defect. Headlines and score labels should not humiliate readers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Publication process</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Define the reader question and what the page will not attempt to answer.</li>
    <li>Collect and verify primary evidence under the <a href="/source-policy/">source policy</a>.</li>
    <li>Draft the page with formulas, definitions, dates, assumptions, and limitations where relevant.</li>
    <li>Check factual claims against their cited sources and test links.</li>
    <li>Review the page for clarity, accessibility, conflicts, safety, and consistency with current product behavior.</li>
    <li>Publish an updated date and revisit material claims when source data or the model changes.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Authorship and review</h2>
  <ContentNote title="No credential claim">
    <p>
      Cooked Finance does not currently claim that its content is reviewed by a
      CFP professional, CPA, attorney, physician, or other credentialed specialist.
      We will not imply professional review until a named reviewer has actually
      reviewed the material and has agreed to a truthful public attribution.
    </p>
  </ContentNote>
  <p>
    When a page has a named author or specialist reviewer, its byline should link
    to a profile explaining relevant experience, role, and potential conflicts.
    Anonymous expertise, invented biographies, stock-photo “experts,” and
    fabricated testimonials are not acceptable.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of assistive tools</h2>
  <p>
    Software, including generative tools, may assist with research organization,
    drafting, editing, code, or accessibility checks. Tool output is not treated
    as a source. Factual claims still require verification, and the publisher is
    responsible for the final page. We do not publish unreviewed bulk-generated
    articles or invent quotations, experience, credentials, or source findings.
  </p>

  <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising or future commercial relationships do not purchase favorable
    editorial coverage, scoring treatment, rankings, links, or access to financial
    inputs. Commercial material must be clearly separated and labelled under our
    <a href="/advertising-policy/">advertising policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    An “updated” date should reflect a meaningful review or change, not a cosmetic
    timestamp refresh. Confirmed material errors are corrected transparently under
    the <a href="/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a>. Readers can report
    a concern through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

